{
  "appendix":"AE",
  "title":"Visa Estimated and Incremental Authorization Transactions",
  "specification":"ATL105",
  "specificationVersion":"2026-3",
  "source":"Appendix AE-1; Appendix I-26 sub-table 09, I-67 through I-72 Table 063; Section 10.4.5; Appendix I-36 Table 044 and K-23 Table 028 as related identifier evidence, not resolved AE wire mapping",
  "applicability":"Logical Visa initial/incremental/completion series, special MCC restrictions and lodging/rental timing. No exhaustive merchant eligibility or full wire contract.",
  "sourceNotes":[
    "4121 and 5411 are CNP-only; 5552 is for EV. These are special restrictions, not an exhaustive allowlist: AE also describes cruise/lodging/vehicle rental and other rental merchants.",
    "Permitted merchants use estimated/initial authorization when final amount is unknown. Example and sub-table 09 specify estimated indicator 1, length 001; incremental requests omit it.",
    "Merchant resends returned approval code; BUYPASS Host identifies incremental and supplies the incremental indicator to Visa. Do not invent a separate merchant incremental flag.",
    "Incremental follows an initial/estimated authorization and retains Sequence Number, Transaction Identifier and Table 063 Terminal Transaction Number. AE leaves Transaction Identifier segment number blank.",
    "Related Table 044 and response Table 028 describe 15-alphanumeric transaction identifiers for COF. This oracle uses that bounded logical evidence shape without claiming they resolve AE's wire placement.",
    "Table 063 data length 011 contains MMDD arrival or four spaces, two-digit duration or two spaces, four-digit terminal transaction number, and P preferred customer or example space-fill.",
    "Terminal number is mandatory for lodging, incremental and EV, unique for a new series, and unchanged within the same-card series until completion. Examples cover lodging, non-T&E and EV initial/incremental/completion.",
    "Completion sends final amount; fixture amounts are parsed nonnegative minor-unit digit strings, not a new currency/amount wire rule.",
    "Cruise/lodging/vehicle rental approvals expire 14 days from initial; other rentals such as trailer parks/campgrounds seven days. Incrementals do not reset the clock. No generic seven-day window for all other merchants.",
    "Longer stays/rentals require completing the first transaction THEN initiating the second on/before applicable day 14/7. Logical elapsed days allow fractional boundaries; real timezone/day-cutoff policy remains external.",
    "Section 10.4.5: original Segment 134 Settlement Type Element 198 X requires Table 021 PINless Debit Acceptance X on associated reversals/completions/incrementals; this profile covers incremental/completion stages.",
    "Examples are same merchant/cardholder; actual series identity, merchant permission, approvals, host-to-Visa behavior and chargebacks are not certified by synthetic fields."
  ],
